  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating the transition to electric mobility in Rwanda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: Disbursement data provided is cumulative and covers disbursement made by the project Agency.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main socio-economic benefits of the project are related to (1) decreasing the country&#x2019;s dependence on imported fuels, liberating resources for economic development and facilitating the stability of transport prices, (2) opening new business and employment opportunities with a strong potential for innovation and professional development as well as for women engagement, (3) contributing to the modernization and affordability of transport systems (including urban mobility) and (4) contributing to the improvement of air quality in Kigali and other cities. The project intends to provide a long-term policy for a quicker transition to electric mobility in Rwanda, reinforced by measures such as the phasing out of the dirtiest and fuel-consuming vehicles.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To accelerate the transition towards electrification of the road transport system in Rwanda, while contributing to the provision of higher quality sustainable mobility options and to the achievement of Rwanda&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x2122;s Nationally Determined Contribution (NDC) GHG emission reduction targets.</narrative>
  </description>
